    "text": "One mole of oxygen gas is made to undergo a process in which its molar heat capacity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> depends on its absolute temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">C</mtext><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">T</mtext></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;is a positive constant. Work done by the gas when heated from an initial temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> to a final temperature&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;will be",
